WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.930
A car engine burns fuel in air.

2
00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:06.030
You might expect the exhaust
to contain carbon dioxide and

3
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.870
water, and it does.

4
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.830
But a sensor in the exhaust
picks up something else too:

5
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.490
oxides of nitrogen.

6
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.970
So where does the nitrogen come from?

7
00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:19.230
And why should anyone care
about a little extra gas?

8
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.430
In this mission, you'll meet the
pollutants released when fuels

9
00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:27.350
burn: carbon monoxide, sulfur
dioxide and oxides of nitrogen.

10
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.290
You'll find out where each one
comes from, what harm it does,

11
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.050
and how some of them cause acid rain.

12
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.860
Your mission: track down
where the nitrogen comes from.
